(755, 'Kew Solar Ltd', 'c-linkinfo@kewsolar.co.uk', 'Unit G03 Courtenay House, 10 Courtenay Road, East Lane Business Park, Wembley, HA9 7ND', '02082 11411', '07944 386622', '7215508', 'logo@2x.png', 'Solar Panel Installers', 'www.kewsolar.co.uk', '<p class=\"myclass\" style=\"font-family: sofia_pro_softlight;\">Kewsolar are specialist Solar PV installers who can install any size system from a domestic house up to large scale commercial buildings. We also install battery systems linked to PV installations. Kewsolar are Part-P Certified; this means we are fully qualified to install electrics on your premises - Part-P is required by law under the building regulations. It ensures that all our electrical fittings will be installed safely, to industry standards and regulations.&nbsp;We are also fully certified installers with over twelve years experience in the solar panel industry. We offer a totally professional service from initial survey through to completion - it is our promise to provide a clear, concise, and ethical service to help you understand the benefits of Solar PV, and how you can earn money from the Government\'s green initiatives. <strong>Is Solar PV right for my Building?</strong>&nbsp;Solar PV is suitable for almost all buildings and homes in urban and rural locations around the UK &mdash; all that is required is some unshaded roof space. The amount of energy received from the sun does vary across the country but not by a large amount. The best position to receive the most direct sunlight is an unshaded, south to south-east facing roof at a 30&deg; slope/pitch. Having a different roof pitch will only marginally effect the amount sunlight reaching the panels. Kewsolar offer a range of Solar PV solutions to suit our clients requirements, including stand-alone, grid-connected, and hybrid solar systems.</p>', 1, 3, '2017-01-30 15:12:43', NULL, NULL, 5),
