(350, 21987, 'Royal Botanic Gardens Lighting Upgrade', 'Kew Estates', '2,000,000.00', 'Jo Lilley', 'J.Lilley@kew.org', '2023-06-30', NULL, 'The works compromised of the replacement of existing luminaires and emergency luminaires in four buildings on the Royal Botanic Gardens Kew site.\r\n\r\nThe four buildings were:\r\n•	Herbarium Building\r\n•	Jodrel Laboratory Building\r\n•	Administration Building\r\n•	Victoria Plaza\r\nThe Works included the survey, design, supply, delivery, offloading, handling into position, erection, co-ordination, supervision, installation, testing, setting to work, commissioning and maintaining for the one-year defects liability period of all the electrical lighting services installation.\r\n\r\nRaytell provided \'As Installed\' record drawings, operation and maintenance information, together with compliance of all preliminary requirements relating to the works such as programming, preparation of working drawings, completion of any specialist design, provision of builder’s work information.\r\n\r\nTestimonial\r\nI have been very pleased with the workmanship and interaction of the Raytell Electrical Team. They have been diligent and forthcoming with ideas to overcome operational issues found within the course of their current project with us. The Administrative and Project management\r\nback-up has been equally as good, with all communications dealt with in a professional and courteous manner. I look forward to a continued working relationship. - Rik Upjohn Kew\r\n \r\n', 'pending', NULL, '2023-09-14 06:05:40', NULL),
