(383, 22305, 'Peckham Rye Station ', 'BAM Nuttall', '220,000.00', 'Benedict O’Looney Architects', 'benny@benedictolooney.co.uk', '2022-08-30', NULL, 'The roof works comprised of stripping off existing coverings to the 4 no Lower Wing Roof areas including slates and lead crown roofs. The reinstatement of previously stripped roof areas in clay interlocking tiles including associated leadwork and new lead roof covering to crown roof areas and to the main high level building installing leadwork to existing stone cornice. Studying the original contract drawings and Victorian photographs, we could see that the four lower roofs were clad in ‘Taylor’s Patent’ roof tiles. These tiles were an innovative Victorian under and over clay tile with roots in ancient Roman Imbrex and Tegula roof tiles.', 'pending', NULL, '2023-09-28 09:57:46', NULL),
